description: Apply when adding or modifying business logic, fixing bugs, changing API behavior, creating tests, modifying test files, or validating application behavior.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing Rules

- New business logic should normally include tests.
- Bug fixes should include a regression test whenever practical.
- Focus tests on behavior, not implementation details.
- Keep unit tests fast and isolated.
- Use integration tests for important database/API flows.
- Avoid excessive mocking.
- Test failure paths in addition to happy paths.
- Authentication and authorization logic must include negative tests.
- Validate boundary cases and invalid input.
- After meaningful code changes, run the relevant tests.
- Do not modify tests merely to make broken behavior pass unless the requirement has genuinely changed.
